WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.830
The context window is the token budget available for instructions, conversation history,

00:00:04.830 --> 00:00:06.715
retrieved material, and generated output.

00:00:06.715 --> 00:00:10.240
Increasing the configured maximum does not automatically improve answers.

00:00:10.240 --> 00:00:14.360
Longer prompts require more prompt ingestion work and expand the key-value cache that

00:00:14.360 --> 00:00:15.540
stores attention state.

00:00:15.540 --> 00:00:18.760
The result can be higher memory use, a longer delay before output,

00:00:18.760 --> 00:00:20.590
and less capacity for concurrency.

00:00:20.590 --> 00:00:23.135
Prompt processing and generation are different phases.

00:00:23.135 --> 00:00:26.500
Measure prompt tokens per second as well as output tokens per second.

00:00:26.500 --> 00:00:30.785
A retrieval workflow may spend most of its time ingesting documents even when generation

00:00:30.785 --> 00:00:31.205
is fast.

00:00:31.205 --> 00:00:34.060
Reusing cached prompt state can help in supported workflows,

00:00:34.060 --> 00:00:36.650
but cache behavior and memory cost vary by runtime.

00:00:36.650 --> 00:00:39.885
For long documents, remove repeated headers, irrelevant sections,

00:00:39.885 --> 00:00:42.615
and low-value history before sending text to the model.

00:00:42.615 --> 00:00:46.680
Retrieval-augmented generation should select the smallest set of relevant passages rather

00:00:46.680 --> 00:00:48.870
than filling the entire context by default.

00:00:48.870 --> 00:00:53.380
Better chunking, ranking, and prompt structure can improve both speed and answer quality.

00:00:53.380 --> 00:00:57.560
Reserve output space so a large input does not leave the model unable to complete its

00:00:57.560 --> 00:00:58.140
response.

00:00:58.140 --> 00:01:01.850
Set context length to the demonstrated requirement and monitor cache growth.

00:01:01.850 --> 00:01:04.055
Test short, normal, and worst-case prompts.

00:01:04.055 --> 00:01:06.380
If performance collapses only on extreme inputs,

00:01:06.380 --> 00:01:10.330
control input size or use a separate batch workflow instead of penalizing every

00:01:10.330 --> 00:01:11.510
interactive request.

00:01:11.510 --> 00:01:15.520
Context is a resource to manage, not a capacity target to maximize.
